==============================
WIDTH, HEIGHT & PERCENTAGES
==============================

1. WIDTH
--------
Width controls how wide an element is (horizontal size).

2. HEIGHT
---------
Height controls how tall an element is (vertical size).

3. WIDTH & HEIGHT with px
-------------------------
px = fixed size (does not change with screen size)

Example:
.box {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
}

4. WIDTH & HEIGHT with %
-------------------------
Percentages depend on the PARENT element's size.

Example:
Parent width = 500px
Child width = 50%  --> 250px

5. WIDTH with %
---------------
Width percentage almost always works because the parent always has a width.

Example:
.parent {
    width: 800px;
}

.child {
    width: 50%;   /* 400px */
}

6. HEIGHT with % (Important Rule)
---------------------------------
Height percentage works ONLY if the parent has a FIXED height.

Works:
.parent {
    height: 300px;
}

.child {
    height: 50%;   /* 150px */
}

Does NOT work:
.parent {
    height: auto;    /* auto = no fixed height */
}

.child {
    height: 50%;     /* cannot calculate 50% of auto */
}

7. Width % Example
------------------
.container {
    width: 1000px;
}

.box {
    width: 25%;    /* 250px */
}

8. Height % Example
-------------------
.container {
    height: 500px;
}

.box {
    height: 20%;    /* 100px */
}

9. width: 100%
--------------
The element fills the entire width of the parent.

If parent = 600px --> child = 600px
If parent = 300px --> child = 300px

10. height: auto
----------------
Height grows depending on the content inside.

11. Why Percentage is Useful
----------------------------
Percentage makes layouts responsive:
- Elements resize as screen changes
- Flexible layouts
- Works well with flexbox and grid

12. SUMMARY (Easy to Remember)
------------------------------
WIDTH:
- px = fixed width
- % = based on parent width
- width: 100% = fill parent width

HEIGHT:
- px = fixed height
- % = works only if parent has fixed height
- height: 100% = fill parent height (only when parent has height)

PERCENTAGES:
- Always relative to parent size
- Width % works easily
- Height % needs fixed parent height
